{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Now come and listen [F]to my [C]story
A [C]story that I know is [G]true
A little [C]rose [F]bloomed in [C]Georgia
[C]With hair of [G]gold and a heart so [C]true
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Way [F]down in the blue ridge [C]mountains
Way [C]down where the tall pines [G]grow
[C]Lives my sweetheart of the [F]mountains
[C]She's my [G]little Georgia [C]rose
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Her mother left her with another
A carefree life she had planned
Baby now is a lady
The one her mother couldn't stand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
We often sing old songs together
I watched her do her little part
She smiled at me when I would tell her
That she was my sweetheart
{end_of_chorus}
